hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1732","**\nNarrated to us Yusuf ibn Musa, who said: Narrated to us Jarir, from Mansur, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Al-Qartha' Ad-Dabbi (RA), who said: \Al-Qartha' was among the early reciters.\"" He narrated from Salman (RA)"," who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n\""O Salman! What is the day of Friday?\""\n\nI replied"," \""Allah and His Messenger know best.\""\n\nHe (ﷺ) asked again"," \""O Salman! What is the day of Friday?\""\n\nI replied"," \""Allah and His Messenger know best.\""\n\nHe (ﷺ) asked a third time"," \""O Salman! What is the day of Friday?\""\n\nI replied"," \""Allah and His Messenger know best.\""\n\nHe (ﷺ) then said: \""O Salman! On Friday"," your father (Adam) or your father's father (Adam) was gathered (created). I will tell you about Friday: When a man performs the purification (ghusl) on Friday as you have been commanded"," then leaves his house and comes to the mosque"," and sits down"," and remains silent until he finishes the prayer"," it will be an expiation for what was between that Friday and the previous one.\""\n\n---"""
